const deps=load("deps");
function internal(id,statement,uses,justification){deps.push({id,category:3,statement,origin:{kind:"derivation",reference:"Basis proof, derivation "+id,revision:"this 2basis submission",evidence:[{input:"problem.md"}]},compatibility:"internal",uses,port:null,lean:null,justification});}
internal("B010","For every metric space X with Borel measurable structure and every p>0: at each finite scale δ>0, YuiContent p (ofReal δ) A is the infimum of sums of ordinary diameter powers over countable δ-covers, with empty members costing zero; it is antitone in δ. The supremum over finite positive δ is μH[p](A). Moreover μH[p](A)=0 iff for every δ>0 and ε>0 there is such a cover of total cost <ofReal ε. Every admissible cover bounds the content from above.",
["B001"],"Expand the content infimum, use monotonicity of the admissible-cover family, cofinality of finite positive scales toward zero, and the defining property of an infimum. The complete order argument and empty-set convention are given in the proof.");
internal("B011","For every metric space X, A⊆X, and real q>0, μH[q](A)=0 implies μH[q+1](A×[0,1])=0 in the standard max product metric on X×ℝ. More quantitatively, for 0<r≤1 and ε>0 one constructs a countable cover of A×[0,1] of diameter at most 2r and (q+1)-cost at most 2^(q+2) ε.",
["B010"],"Choose an r/2-cover of cost <ε/2. Enlarge its diameter numbers slightly to positive radii a_i≤r with total q-power <ε. Cover each nonempty member by a closed a_i-ball around one of its points, and use ceil(1/a_i) equal subintervals. The proof supplies the radii budgets, cardinality bound, diameter bound and cost calculation. No positive actual diameter or positive-dimensional ambient space is assumed.");
internal("B012","For every metric space X, A⊆X, real s>0 and δ>0, YuiContent s (ofReal δ) A ≤ YuiContent (s+1) (ofReal δ) (A×[0,1]) in the standard max product metric. Consequently μH[s](A)≤μH[s+1](A×[0,1]).",
["B010","B006","B007","B009"],"Project each arbitrary δ-cover to X and ℝ. Enlarge each bounded real projection to a measurable open interval with error η_i=ε·2^(-i-1)/(1+ρ_i^s). Integrate the pointwise content bound over [0,1], obtaining c≤∑ρ_i^(s+1)+ε. Let ε decrease to zero, then infimize over covers and take suprema over scales. The proof handles empty members and ∞ explicitly; it does not assume projected sets are measurable.");
internal("B013","For every finite dimensional real normed space V and every nonempty compact E⊆V, with the standard max product metric, dimH(E×[0,1])=dimH E+1 (equality in ℝ≥0∞). This includes finrankℝ V=0.",
["B002","B003","B004","B005","B011","B012"],"The ambient bound makes D=dimH E finite. For q>D, B002 and B011 give zero (q+1)-measure and hence the upper dimension bound; pass q↓D. If D>0 use B012 and infinite s-measure for 0<s<D, then s↑D. If D=0 embed the unit interval isometrically using a point of E. Full limiting order arguments occur in the proof.");
internal("B014","For each natural n (including zero), identify V=EuclideanSpace ℝ (Fin n) with Euclidean ℝ^n. Let T:V×ℝ→EuclideanSpace ℝ (Fin(n+1)) be the real linear bijection with T(x,t)(0)=t and T(x,t)(i.succ)=x(i). For every E⊆V, dimH(T '' (E×[0,1]))=dimH(E×[0,1]) computed in the standard max product on the right. Hence B013 proves the original Euclidean target for every nonempty compact E⊆ℝ^n.",
["B008","B013"],"Define the inverse by x(i)=z(i.succ), t=z(0); finite-index case analysis proves both inverse laws and coordinate algebra proves linearity. Domain and codomain are finite dimensional real normed spaces, so the prepared B008 adapter applies. A coordinate permutation from first to last interval coordinate is a linear equivalence as well. The proof also gives explicit max-versus-Euclidean metric bounds.");
store("deps",deps);
